From ccc60e62abf57303a488e46ad76959b6553f5abb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:41:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] common: close the n_seq_max == 1 gap in --fit's auto-context
 probe, cap iGPU free memory consistently

13cdadfc9's clamp only ran inside `if (n_seq_max > 1)` -- a leftover
scope from chasing the exact reproduction (n_parallel=auto, which is
always > 1). With `--parallel 1` and no `-c`, the probe still measures
at the model's full native n_ctx_train with zero protection: no clamp,
no backoff loop. K2-Horizon-7B's n_ctx_train (524288) is large on its
own regardless of n_seq_max, so this device class does not need a
multiplier to hit the same real-memory overshoot 13cdadfc9 fixed for
n_seq_max > 1.

Fix: dropped the n_seq_max > 1 condition so the pre-probe clamp and
the exception backoff loop both run whenever n_ctx_auto, for any
n_seq_max. Nothing inside that block actually depended on n_seq_max --
it only sizes n_ctx_max via n_seq_max before entering the block, same
as before. One path now protects both cases instead of two.

Second gap: the clamp's iGPU host-free cap was local to that one
clamp computation. Every other place in common_params_fit_impl that
sizes something from a dmds_t's .free -- the initial probe's targets,
the MoE cpu-offload surplus check -- read the device's own (possibly
inflated) figure straight, uncapped. A UMA device could pass the
pre-probe clamp on an honest host-free reading and still have the
function's later per-device `targets[id] = dmds_full[id].free -
margins[id]` (used to decide how many layers get offloaded to it)
work from the uncapped figure, silently reopening the same class of
overshoot the clamp exists to prevent.

Extracted the cap into a pure, unit-testable function,
common_fit_cap_igpu_free(dev_free, host_free, is_igpu), mirroring
common_fit_clamp_ctx_to_free_memory()'s existing pure-core/thin-wrapper
split. A static common_fit_cap_igpu_free_to_host() wrapper applies it
to every device in a dmds_t using its own trailing host entry, and is
now called right after every common_get_device_memory_data_impl() call
in common_params_fit_impl() whose result feeds a free-memory-based
decision: the initial step-1 probe, the pre-probe clamp's own
minimum-context measurement, the probe after the backoff loop, and the
MoE dense/cpu-offload surplus check. (get_memory_for_layers()'s calls
use only .mb.total(), never .free, so they need no cap.)

Verification (workstation only, Intel UHD 770 iGPU, same
`systemd-run --scope -p MemoryMax=10G -p MemorySwapMax=0`, one process
at a time, `free -g` checked before each, per this session's standing
rule against touching cluster nodes):
- `--parallel 1`, no `-c`, K2-Horizon-7B: before this commit, this
  path had no clamp at all (n_ctx_max = 524288, n_seq_max == 1 skipped
  the whole block); after, logs "clamping the auto-context probe from
  524288 to 102495" against real device free memory, then (with
  -fitt 13000 to match this test's own 10G cap, same reasoning as
  13cdadfc9's verification) settles at 16060 and serves a real
  completion.
- n_parallel=auto (the original regression case), no `-c`: still
  clamps (2097152 -> 16736 with the same -fitt) and serves a real
  completion -- confirms the refactor did not regress the case
  13cdadfc9 fixed.
- Explicit `-c 8192`: no clamp log line (gated on n_ctx_auto), starts
  and serves a completion identically to before.
- ctest -L main: 60/60. ctest -R split-balance: 1/1.
- tests/test-fit-clamp.cpp: added 3 cases for
  common_fit_cap_igpu_free() (non-iGPU passthrough, iGPU capped down
  to host_free, iGPU under host_free left alone).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
